  "problem": "$(8u-3v)\\cdot (-6)=${{field-1}}\n$u\\,+$\n{{field-2}}\n$v$",
  "worked_solution": "Using the distributive law, we multiply each term inside the parentheses by the number $(-6):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(8u-3v)\\cdot (-6) & = \\\\ 8u\\cdot (-6)+(-3v)\\cdot (-6) & = \\\\ (-48u)+(18v) & = \\\\ -48u+18v & \\end{aligned}\n$$",
